WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.467
-Welcome back, everybody.
We're talking with

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.534
one of my favorites,
Liam Neeson, right here.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:09.067
He stars in the new film,
"Blacklight."

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.200
Let's talk about "Blacklight."

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.400
This is written
by Mark Williams.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.434
-Mark Williams.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.901
-Go ahead. Uh-huh.

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:18.400
-What are you reaching for?
I'm going to get spot out here.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.968
-Rather than me go,
"What is the film about?"

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:24.267
Uh, well, it is about me
doing a -- okay.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:26.000
Here it is.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.300
You came prepared, yeah.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.534
-"Blacklight" --
-You're not even off-script.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:29.968
-Do you mind me doing this?
-No, I don't mind.

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:33.234
-"Blacklight" offers the kind of
high-octane thrills

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:35.367
people associate
with Liam Neeson,

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:38.701
uniquely combined with a mature,
political edge.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.868
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:43.334
This is very much a film
about uncovering

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:46.634
corruption at the highest levels
of government power

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.434
and the decision to stop blindly
following

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:52.200
corrupt leaders while
reexamining

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.868
one's set of inner morals."

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:55.968
-Wow.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:58.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:00.234
Next time you come on,
I would like you

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.367
to just read the phone book.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.100
It still would sound amazing.
Yeah.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.133
-And there's thrills and spills,
you know.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.100
-Yeah, there's thrills
and spills, but this is --

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.534
the guy is behind "Ozark,"
which is one of the best shows.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:11.534
-I love "Ozark."

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:12.901
-Ever. Are you caught up?

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.133
-I love it. Yes.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:16.400
I can't -- Laura Linney
is a good friend of mine.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.701
Ah, stuff it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:22.234
And I called her up,
I sent her a message saying,

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:25.601
"Laura, I'm finished,
series four, part one.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.200
When is part two coming out?"

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.400
-You did that?
-Yeah.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.067
-I didn't do that.
-And she said, "April."

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.501
And I thought,
"Okay, this is February."

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.400
And then I got in touch
with Mark Williams and I said,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.834
"Mark, when is part two
coming out?"

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:38.501
And he says, "Oh, autumn,
the fall."

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.567
-You go, "Hey, I thought we were
friends."

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.934
Yeah, I need this. I keep
stretching it out because I go,

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.033
"I don't want the show to end."

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.200
-I love it.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.334
-Anyways, this movie's
everything you want.

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:48.834
It's pure entertainment.

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:49.868
It's Liam Neeson.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:50.868
It's a popcorn movie.

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.033
It's awesome.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:53.133
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:55.167
Liam Neeson, "Blacklight."
Take a look.

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:59.601
♪♪

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:02.501
-Based on the fact these crazies
are about to bury you

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:05.100
in a shallow grave,
something happened.

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:08.901
-I've been out here
almost two years

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:11.767
playing a part
with these racist bastards,

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:15.167
and it's getting inside my head.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.234
I got sloppy.

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:18.701
They found a few bugs.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.968
They somehow traced it back
to me.

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.601
-Stop it,
Special Agent Davidson.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:26.167
I need you to keep your wits
intact.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:28.033
-i thought it was your job

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.100
to get me out of this kind of
situation.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.267
-That is correct.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:33.434
And I'm about to.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.634
-That's exactly right!

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:36.667
Yes!

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:37.868
Liam Neeson, everybody.

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.801
"Blacklight" opens in theaters
February 11th.

